ss risk up to its end; I accept that.\n3. Canary 2 keeps priority for your attention when a phase needs you.\n' "$N" > leg_s1_canary/inbox/${N}_ORCH_ORDER_fix_wrapper_slot_copy.md; printf '# ORCH (%s): the production wrapper\x27s slot copy has an integrity bug; do not install a new wrapper from the current template yet\nleg_s1_canary reproduced it (`leg_s1_canary/out/LIVE_SLOT_RACE_REPRO.json`): when tar fails, the wrapper still marks the archive verified, because no stage of the pipeline is checked and the re-read proves only the checksum of what was written. leg_s1_canary delivers a patch to `work/adm/jl5_template.sh` with tests; I have it reviewed once; you then install the reviewed copy as the wrapper for the next kit. Until then, prepare everything else for the next kit as usual, but the wrapper is not ready. Never run the slot block while training runs.\n' "$N" > orchard_cp2/inbox/${N}_ORCH_wrapper_slot_copy_bug.md; echo "$(date -u +%FT%TZ) orch-home-distill-79: leg_s1_canary RESULT 1058Z: (a) the unchanged production slot block must not run during training (inline, after job.sh, no lock or snapshot; rotating saves move all but the newest two states into _superseded); (b) INTEGRITY BUG in the production wrapper and the next template: tar exit 2 is never checked, so an archive holding only inputs/ and binding.json is marked verified and the wrapper exits 0 (repro leg_s1_canary/out/LIVE_SLOT_RACE_REPRO.json). RULING: fix is a production-GO blocker: canary lane patches the wrapper template (pipeline status checks, content verification, verified only after both, restore refuses unchecked records) with fixture tests; one independent review; orchard_cp2 installs the reviewed copy. Live mid-allocation copy deferred to the continuation; node-loss risk accepted for the first allocation." >> ORCH_HANDOFF.md